* {{audio|en|en-us-minister.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-minister.ogg|a=UK}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mey- (small)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|ministre}}, from {{der|en|fro|ministre}}, from {{der|en|la|minister||an attendant, servant, assistant, a priest's assistant or other under official}}, from {{m|la|minor||less}} + {{m|la|-ter}}; see [[minor]]. {{doublet|en|Minorite}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|cleric}} {{lb|en|religion}} A person who is trained to preach, to perform religious ceremonies, and to afford [[pastoral]] care at a [[Protestant]] [[church]].
#: {{hyper|en|cleric}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''minister''' said a prayer on behalf of the entire [[congregation]].}}
# {{senseid|en|government}} {{lb|en|government}} A politician who heads a [[ministry]]
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:government minister}}
#: {{hyper|en|provost<qq:chief minister in areas of Central Europe and Scandinavia>}}
#: {{ux|en|He was newly appointed to be '''Minister''' of the Interior.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1661 (first printed)|author=w:Francis Bacon|title=A Letter of Advice to the Duke of Buckingham|text='''Ministers''' to kings, whose eyes, ears, and hands they are, must be answerable to God and man.}}
# {{senseid|en|diplomacy}} In [[diplomacy]], the rank of diplomat directly below [[ambassador]].
# {{senseid|en|servant}} A [[servant]]; a [[subordinate]]; an [[officer]] or [[assistant]] of [[inferior]] [[rank]]; hence, an [[agent]], an [[instrument]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|act=III|scene=ii|page=287|column=2|passage={{nb...}}, I choſe&nbsp;/ ''Camillo'' for the '''miniſter''', to poyſon&nbsp;/ My friend ''Polixenes:'' {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Exodus|24|13|page=162|column=1|text=And Moſes roſe vp, and his '''miniſter''' Ioſhua: and Moſes went vp into the mount of God.}}

